  "summary": "A planned semiconductor assembly and test plant near Wrocław, Poland, announced in June 2023 with investment of up to $4.6 billion and about 2,000 Intel jobs, meant to meet demand Intel expected by 2027. Construction was to follow European Commission approval, and Intel's April 2024 update still listed the plant as planned. Intel paused the project by about two years in September 2024 and dropped it in July 2025.",
